Revision history for Perl extension Ushuffle.

0.02
	- new interface: shuffle($sequence, $k) returns the shuffled string,
	  Ushuffle::Shuffler gives repeated shuffles of one sequence, and
	  set_seed seeds the random number generator
	- removed shuffle($s, $t, $l, $k), shuffle1 and shuffle2, which wrote
	  into a caller-supplied buffer without checking its size
	- the random number generator is seeded when the module is loaded
	- bundled library updated to https://github.com/s-will/ushuffle v1.2.2
	  plus a fix for an integer overflow in the hash function on sequences
	  of tens of millions of characters
	- the library is compiled as part of the extension; the module files
	  are no longer generated with h2xs

0.01
	- original version; created by h2xs 1.23 with options
		-O -n Ushuffle ./Ushuffle/ushufflelib/ushuffle.h
